  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Psalms",
    "delineation": "Psalm",
    "number": 4,
    "summary": "David pleads for mercy—He counsels, Put your trust in the Lord.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "Hear me when I call, O God of my righteousness: thou hast enlarged me when I was in distress; have mercy upon me, and hear my prayer.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 4,
            "text": "Ps. 34:4; Micah 7:7; 1 Jn. 5:14 (13–14); Mosiah 9:18; Ether 1:40 (39–40)."
          },
          {
            "start": 33,
            "end": 46,
            "text": "Ps. 97:6 (5–6); Rom. 1:17; 2 Ne. 4:35; Ether 9:22; D&C 1:16."
          },
          {
            "start": 84,
            "end": 92,
            "text": "Gen. 35:3; Ps. 118:5 (4–6); Isa. 25:4 (1, 4)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 70,
            "end": 80
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "O ye sons of men, how long will ye turn my glory into shame? how long will ye love vanity, and seek after leasing? Selah.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 54,
            "end": 59,
            "text": "TG Shame."
          },
          {
            "start": 83,
            "end": 89,
            "text": "TG Vanity."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 39
          },
          {
            "start": 61,
            "end": 69
          },
          {
            "start": 91,
            "end": 94
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "But know that the Lord hath set apart him that is godly for himself: the Lord will hear when I call unto him.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 37,
            "text": "TG Setting Apart."
          },
          {
            "start": 50,
            "end": 55,
            "text": "TG Godliness."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Stand in awe, and sin not: commune with your own heart upon your bed, and be still. Selah.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Offer the sacrifices of righteousness, and put your trust in the Lord.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 10,
            "end": 20,
            "text": "TG Sacrifice."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "There be many that say, Who will shew us any good? Lord, lift thou up the light of thy countenance upon us.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 87,
            "end": 98,
            "text": "Ps. 67:1; 119:135; Alma 5:14; 3 Ne. 19:25 (24–25)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 8
          },
          {
            "start": 41,
            "end": 44
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "Thou hast put gladness in my heart, more than in the time that their corn and their wine increased.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 69,
            "end": 73,
            "text": "HEB grain."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 58,
            "end": 62
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": []
      },
      {
        "text": "I will both lay me down in peace, and sleep: for thou, Lord, only makest me dwell in safety.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 27,
            "end": 32,
            "text": "TG Contentment."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": []
      }
    ]
  },
